    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0505" n="219" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg219"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857B46</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-01T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 1, 1916, 3 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2873. Department is informed that British steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Berwindvale</hi>, carrying four Americans, was torpedoed without warning on
                    March 16 off Bantry, Ireland. The vessel was apparently returning to the United
                    States for cargo.</p>
                <p>Please bring this to the attention of the German Government with request to be
                    informed whether this vessel was torpedoed by a submarine belonging to Germany
                    or her allies. It is expected that a prompt answer will be given.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
